      "id": 1,
      "text": "North Plainfield was first inhabited by the Lenni Lenape, Algonquian‑speaking indigenous peoples, long before European settlers arrived.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/North_Plainfield,_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Dutch families such as the Vermeule and Cadmus settled the area before the American Revolution, laying early foundations for the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/North_Plainfield,_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "North Plainfield Township incorporated in 1872 from portions of larger townships, later becoming a distinct borough.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/North_Plainfield,_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the 1880s, North Plainfield’s industrial growth lagged behind neighboring Plainfield, which boasted hat factories, printing presses, and carriage shops.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/North_Plainfield,_New_Jersey",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 1950s Silk Palace barbershop on Plainfield Avenue, owned by George Clinton, became a hub for Parliament‑Funkadelic members and local musicians.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plainfield%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 2022, a stretch of Plainfield Avenue was officially renamed Parliament Funkadelic Way to honor the town’s rich musical heritage.",
